hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1513","I am Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi, from Ismail bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala al-Aslami. H Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Sabah narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Wahib narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala narrated to us. H Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala. Al-Aslami, on the authority of Abu Ali Al-Hamdani, said: I heard Uqba bin Amir, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever... If the time came, and the prayer was completed, then it is for him and for them, and whoever detracts from that, it is on him and not on them.” This is the hadith of Ibn Wahb, and the meaning of their hadiths is the same."
